WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.867 --> 00:00:15.965
Heidi reached the field of flowers and uttered a cry of joy.

2
00:00:15.966 --> 00:00:21.837
Peter, who was nearby with the flock of goats, heard her and turned to look.

3
00:00:21.838 --> 00:00:27.083
The whole ground in front of Heidi was filled with gold and yellow blossoms.

4
00:00:27.084 --> 00:00:32.229
Above the gold flowers grew thick bushes of deep blue flowers.

5
00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:36.153
Heidi turned around and ran back to Clara's side.

6
00:00:36.154 --> 00:00:41.348
"Oh, you must come, you must," said Heidi excitedly.

7
00:00:41.349 --> 00:00:45.673
"It is more beautiful than you can imagine."

8
00:00:45.674 --> 00:00:49.901
"But Heidi, how?" asked Clara.

9
00:00:49.902 --> 00:00:53.256
"I will help you!" said Heidi.

10
00:00:53.257 --> 00:00:56.145
"But you are smaller than me.

11
00:00:56.146 --> 00:01:00.979
Oh, if only I could walk!" said Clara.

12
00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.888
Suddenly, Heidi had an idea.

13
00:01:03.889 --> 00:01:09.393
"Peter, Peter, come down here!" she yelled.

14
00:01:09.394 --> 00:01:13.683
"No, I don't want to," Peter replied.

15
00:01:13.684 --> 00:01:16.008
"I cannot do it alone.

16
00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:18.692
You must come and help me."

17
00:01:18.693 --> 00:01:24.200
"No, I shall do nothing of the kind," said Peter angrily.

18
00:01:24.201 --> 00:01:27.800
Heidi ran up to where Peter sat and said,

19
00:01:27.801 --> 00:01:33.576
"If you don't come at once, Peter, I will do something you won't like!"

20
00:01:33.577 --> 00:01:39.913
Heidi had no idea what she might do, but she was angry at Peter's stubbornness.

21
00:01:39.914 --> 00:01:42.218
Peter was suddenly afraid.

22
00:01:42.219 --> 00:01:50.158
Maybe, just maybe, Heidi knew that he had destroyed Clara's wheelchair and was planning to tell someone.

23
00:01:50.159 --> 00:01:56.598
"If I come, will you promise not to do what you said?" asked Peter carefully.

24
00:01:56.599 --> 00:02:01.728
"Yes," said Heidi, and so they both went back to Clara.

25
00:02:01.729 --> 00:02:10.587
Heidi told Peter to hold her up on one side, while she took the other, and together they helped Clara to her feet.

26
00:02:10.588 --> 00:02:16.451
So far, so good, but Clara could not keep upright without support.

27
00:02:16.452 --> 00:02:20.539
"Put your arm around my neck," Heidi told her.

28
00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.825
"Peter, give her your arm."

29
00:02:22.826 --> 00:02:32.671
Peter had never done anything like this before, so Heidi showed him how to make a crook with his arm that Clara could lean on.

30
00:02:32.672 --> 00:02:36.086
Still, they were not very successful.

31
00:02:36.087 --> 00:02:42.334
Peter was taller than Heidi, so Clara was unbalanced and flopped heavily between them.

32
00:02:42.335 --> 00:02:47.881
"Try putting one foot down firmly," Heidi advised her.

33
00:02:47.882 --> 00:02:52.152
Cautiously, Clara tried it.

34
00:02:52.153 --> 00:02:57.141
"That didn't hurt nearly as much as I thought it would," she said.

35
00:02:57.142 --> 00:03:04.746
"Try again," urged Heidi, and Clara placed her other foot, then managed several steps.

36
00:03:04.747 --> 00:03:09.122
"Oh Heidi," she cried. "Look at me.

37
00:03:09.123 --> 00:03:12.754
I'm walking! I'm walking!"

38
00:03:12.755 --> 00:03:20.154
Clara still kept hold of Heidi and Peter, but with each step they could feel her getting steadier on her feet.

39
00:03:20.155 --> 00:03:24.143
They didn't have far to go to reach the field of flowers.

40
00:03:24.144 --> 00:03:32.923
When they all sat down among the flowers of gold and blue, Heidi felt so glad at heart that she wanted to shout for joy.

41
00:03:32.924 --> 00:03:37.667
They were all hungry, since it was long past noon.

42
00:03:37.668 --> 00:03:44.705
They ate their lunch, and soon after they finished, Heidi spotted Grandfather climbing up to get them.

43
00:03:44.706 --> 00:03:53.222
She ran to him to tell him the news about Clara and was so excited that she could hardly get the words out.

44
00:03:53.223 --> 00:03:56.998
"So you fought the battle and won the day, did you?"

45
00:03:56.999 --> 00:04:00.194
Grandfather said to Clara when he reached her.

46
00:04:00.195 --> 00:04:05.785
He helped her up and made her walk a few steps, putting one arm around her waist

47
00:04:05.786 --> 00:04:11.984
and holding his other arm firmly in front of her so that she could hold on to it.

48
00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:16.770
With this support, she walked with more confidence than before.

49
00:04:16.771 --> 00:04:23.417
Heidi skipped joyfully beside them, and the old man looked as though a great happiness had come to him.

50
00:04:23.418 --> 00:04:26.518
"You have worked hard enough for today.

51
00:04:26.519 --> 00:04:29.972
You can try again tomorrow," he said.

52
00:04:29.973 --> 00:04:38.848
He then lifted her up onto his back, and off they went, down the mountainside.
